{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790978228,"nonce":"pAWcWKtdsYFYBGlDg3e/CZ+oKMk=","title":"Port the rest of Blinc's primitive shaders to HXSL","message":"c38686f ports only what a Div uses today: sdf_core's rect path (uniform border, two-stop gradient, rect clip) and sdf_shadow's PRIM_SHADOW.\n\nNot yet ported, in rough order of use:\n- per-side border widths and colours (BorderSides; Blinc draws differing colours as 4 rects under a rounded clip);\n- corner shapes (superellipse n: squircle, bevel, scoop, notch — sd_shaped_rect and the superellipse inner corner);\n- transforms: local_affine about the centre and the inverse in the fragment shader; quad expansion to the transformed AABB;\n- inner shadows and circle shadows (sdf_shadow types 4-6), spread on shadows larger than 3x blur;\n- clip_fade (overflow fade) and circle/ellipse/polygon clips;\n- CSS filters (filter_a/filter_b) and mask gradients;\n- outline (stroke_rect with transparent fill);\n- opacity layers (Blinc composites a subtree offscreen when opacity applies to a group, rather than multiplying alpha down);\n- glass, blur and image brushes (separate Blinc pipelines).\n\nAdd each as a module in the UiShader family (Sdf helpers or a new shader), and extend the record from GpuPrimitive's field order. Watch the 16-attribute limit: the record is 12 vec4s now; past that, move to a storage buffer as Blinc's tier 1.","files":null}]}